## End to end user flow

### Signup and onboarding

```
1. User visits beacon.com (Next.js landing)
   → Clicks "Start free"
   → /register page
   → POST /api/auth/register
   → bcrypt hash password
   → INSERT INTO users
   → JWT issued (access 15min + refresh 30d)
   → Redirect to /onboarding

2. /onboarding Step 1 — Connect GitHub
   → GET /api/github/install-url (JWT required; state = userId)
   → Redirect to https://github.com/apps/{GITHUB_APP_NAME}/installations/new
   → User approves read-only access
   → GitHub redirects to {API_URL}/api/github/callback?installation_id=…&state={userId}

3. API callback handler
   → UPSERT github_installations
   → UPDATE scan_status = 'scanning'
   → signalCollectQueue.add('scan', { installation_id, installationDbId, userId })
   → Redis PUBLISH scan-progress:{userId} (live onboarding updates)
   → Redirect to {FRONTEND_URL}/onboarding?step=3

4. Frontend onboarding progress (Step 3)
   → EventSource GET /api/github/onboarding/stream (SSE, not polling)
   → Fallback poll: GET /api/github/onboarding/status
   → Shows live counter "Analysing scanned/total packages…"
   → When scan_status = 'complete' → advance to step 4
   → Step 4 summary → "Go to dashboard"

5. Onboarding Step 2 — Select repos (shipped)
   → GET /api/repos lists GitHub-accessible repos for the installation
   → User picks repos up to plan limit (Starter = 1, Pro = 5)
   → PATCH /api/repos/selected { repoIds: [...] }
   → Stored on github_installations.selectedRepos (JSON array of repo UUIDs)
   → Only selected repos are scanned, listed on dashboard, and included in alerts
```

