### Signal collection worker — what runs in the background

```
5. Signal collect worker picks up job (runs inside API process via startWorkers())

   Scope: ONLY repos in installation.selectedRepos (not all GitHub-granted repos)

   For each selected repo:
   → Walk GitHub file tree
   → Find package.json, pyproject.toml, composer.json,
     requirements.txt, go.mod, pom.xml, Gemfile, Cargo.toml
   → Parse every dependency
   → UPSERT packages (unique on name + ecosystem — shared across all users)
   → UPSERT repo_packages (link repo ↔ package + declared version)

   For each package (concurrent batches):
   → GitHub REST against the MONITORED REPO (not upstream package repo yet):
       commit_velocity_30d, days_since_last_commit
       top contributor login, contributor count
       open/closed issues → close rate, stale ratio
       stars, forks, fork/star ratio
   → Stubs (hardcoded until external APIs wired):
       funding_sponsor_count (always 0)
       ossf_score (placeholder)

   Normalise raw values → six 0–100 scores:
     commitVelocity, maintainerActivity, funding,
     issueResolution, communityHealth, securityHygiene

   Persist:
   INSERT INTO package_signals (signalType, value, rawValue, rawData, source)
     signalType keys: commit_velocity_30d, maintainer_activity,
       funding_sponsor_count, issue_close_rate, fork_star_ratio, ossf_score
     rawData: { facts, maintainers } — contextual copy for UI (on new scans)

   Cache in Redis:
     SET signals:{packageId} EX 21600
     Payload: { ...6 scores, facts, maintainers }

   Structured logs:
     signals_cached_redis, intelligence_score_enqueued

   Update scan_progress.scanned++

   Enqueue intelligence queue:
   intelligenceQueue.add('score', {
     package_id,
     installation_id,          // DB uuid
     installation_github_id,   // GitHub numeric id
     prev_sps: pkg.currentSps, // null on first scan
     signals: {
       commit_velocity, maintainer_activity, funding,
       issue_resolution, community_health, security_hygiene
     }
   })
```

**API resolution layer** (`resolvePackageSignals.service.ts`):
- Package list, detail, and dashboard critical feed call this before responding
- Reads Redis cache first; falls back to latest `package_signals` rows per type
- Maps DB signalType snake_case → camelCase for the frontend
- Returns `{ ...normalized, facts, maintainers }` when available
```

