### Intelligence worker — scoring and prediction

```
6. Intelligence worker picks up job (Python — NOT IN THIS REPO YET)

   Expected: separate FastAPI service (port 5000 locally)
   Consumes: BullMQ queue "intelligence-score" (same Redis as Node)
   Env: INTERNAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET for callback auth

   Build feature vector from job payload (6 × 0–100 scores)

   XGBoost inference → sps (0–100), tier (critical/at-risk/watch/healthy)

   Prediction engine (subsequent scans):
   SELECT last N package_scores → linear regression
   → predicted_critical_at, prediction_confidence (R² gate)

   Reason generation → prediction_reason (LLM or template)

   Recommendation engine → top 3 healthy alternatives (same ecosystem)
   Should UPSERT recommendations table — Node callback ignores this today

   Call back Node.js (required to unblock UI + alerts):
   POST /api/internal/score-complete
   Header: x-internal-secret: {INTERNAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET}
   body: {
     package_id, installation_id,
     new_sps, tier, prev_sps, prev_tier,
     prediction_reason, recommendations, signals
   }

   Node → incrementScanScored():
   UPDATE packages (currentSps, tier, predictionReason)
   INSERT package_scores
   scan_progress.scored++
   checkAndFireAlert() — skipped when prev_sps is null

   ⚠ CURRENT GAP: No Python worker running → jobs accumulate in Redis,
     SPS/tier stay null, alerts never fire, recommendations empty.
```

