GITHUB_APP_NAME=beacon          → install URL slug
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=…      → PEM file in backend/ (preferred locally)
  OR GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=…      → inline PEM with \n escapes (CI/Docker alt)

GitHub App settings (developer):
  Setup URL / Callback: http://localhost:4000/api/github/callback
  Webhook URL (optional locally): needs public URL (ngrok/staging)
  GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=…      → only if webhooks enabled

Optional (not used by current install flow):
  GITHUB_CLIENT_ID, GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET

Docker: backend/docker-compose.yml mounts the PEM read-only into /app/
  and runs scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh → prisma db push + prisma generate + API
```

Permissions: Metadata (read), Contents (read), Issues (read). Event: push (rescan on manifest change).

Internal callback (intelligence → Node):
```
INTERNAL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=…   → required for POST /api/internal/score-complete
```

Prisma: pinned to v6 (`url` + `directUrl` in backend/prisma/schema.prisma). IDE may show false Prisma 7 warnings — use `.vscode/settings.json` prisma.pinToPrisma6.

